\newlabel{fig:bias-variance-mse}{{6.5}{87}{The bias--variance trade-off behind ridge. As shrinkage $\lambda $ rises from zero, the estimator variance (green) falls while the squared bias (red) rises from zero. Their sum, the mean squared error (blue), traces a U-shape; the minimum sits at a strictly positive $\lambda $, so some shrinkage always beats OLS}{figure.6.5}{}}
