\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.3}{\ignorespaces Variogram in log-log coordinates for three Hurst exponent values. The red line and data points ($H = 0.1$) show the flat slope characteristic of rough volatility: variance of increments grows very slowly with lag. The blue dashed line ($H = 0.5$) shows standard Brownian motion with a steep slope of 1.0. The gap between the two slopes quantifies how much standard diffusion models underestimate the persistence of volatility.}}{99}{figure.7.3}\protected@file@percent }
