\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.4}{\ignorespaces ATM implied volatility term structure under two regimes. In normal conditions (\textcolor {defblue}{blue}), the term structure slopes upward as longer horizons carry greater uncertainty. During crises (\textcolor {warnred}{red dashed}), the term structure inverts: near-term IV spikes while long-term IV reflects the expectation that volatility will eventually normalize. The spread between short-dated and long-dated ATM IV is itself a useful feature for forecasting models.}}{116}{figure.8.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:iv-term-structure}{{8.4}{116}{ATM implied volatility term structure under two regimes. In normal conditions (\textcolor {defblue}{blue}), the term structure slopes upward as longer horizons carry greater uncertainty. During crises (\textcolor {warnred}{red dashed}), the term structure inverts: near-term IV spikes while long-term IV reflects the expectation that volatility will eventually normalize. The spread between short-dated and long-dated ATM IV is itself a useful feature for forecasting models}{figure.8.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:iv-term-structure@cref}{{[figure][4][8]8.4}{[1][115][]116}{}{}{}}
