\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19.1}{\ignorespaces Schematic Sharpe-vs-cost curves. Each forecast starts at its gross Sharpe (intercept at $c = 0$) and slides down a straight line whose steepness is its turnover; where a line hits zero is its breakeven cost $c^\ast $. The reactive ML forecast has the highest gross Sharpe but the steepest slope, so it crosses zero first. At the realistic SPX cost ($\approx 1$~bp, dashed line) all three are comfortably positive and the higher gross Sharpe wins.}}{352}{figure.19.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sharpe-cost-curve}{{19.1}{352}{Schematic Sharpe-vs-cost curves. Each forecast starts at its gross Sharpe (intercept at $c = 0$) and slides down a straight line whose steepness is its turnover; where a line hits zero is its breakeven cost $c^\ast $. The reactive ML forecast has the highest gross Sharpe but the steepest slope, so it crosses zero first. At the realistic SPX cost ($\approx 1$~bp, dashed line) all three are comfortably positive and the higher gross Sharpe wins}{figure.19.1}{}}
